var VA_CONTENT_EXPANSION = {"version":"2026-11-09","entries":[{"lesson":0,"title":"Ratios & Unit Rates","bg":[["A part-to-part ratio and a fraction of the whole answer different questions. If a trail mix has 3 cups of oats and 2 cups of raisins, oats : raisins is 3 : 2, but oats make up 3/5 of the mixture. Name the quantities before calculating; the whole is 3 + 2 = 5 cups.","部分与部分的比和某部分占整体的分数回答不同的问题。若混合零食有 3 杯燕麦和 2 杯葡萄干，燕麦 : 葡萄干是 3 : 2，但燕麦占混合物的 3/5。计算前先说明比较的量；整体是 3 + 2 = 5 杯。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Compare on the same basis:\u003c/b> A 750 mL bottle costs $3; a 1 L bottle costs $3.60. Convert 1 L to 1,000 mL, then compare cost per 100 mL: $3 ÷ 7.5 = $0.40 and $3.60 ÷ 10 = $0.36. The second bottle costs less per equal amount. Comparing $3 with $3.60 alone ignores the different sizes.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>用同一单位比较：\u003c/b>750 毫升一瓶售价 3 美元，1 升一瓶售价 3.60 美元。先把 1 升换成 1,000 毫升，再比较每 100 毫升的价钱：$3 ÷ 7.5 = $0.40，$3.60 ÷ 10 = $0.36。第二瓶每份等量饮料更便宜。只比较 3 美元和 3.60 美元忽略了容量不同。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["part-to-whole ratio","部分与整体的比","A comparison of one part with the total. With 3 red and 2 blue tiles, red : all is 3 : 5.","某一部分与总量的比较。3 块红砖、2 块蓝砖中，红砖 : 全部是 3 : 5。"],["rate units","比率的单位","The labels that tell what a rate compares. Dollars per notebook and notebooks per dollar are different rates.","说明比率比较什么的单位。美元/本和本/美元是不同的比率。"]],"q":[["A bracelet has 4 green beads and 6 white beads. What fraction of all the beads is green?","手链有 4 颗绿珠和 6 颗白珠。绿珠占全部珠子的几分之几？",[["2/3","2/3"],["2/5","2/5"],["3/5","3/5"]],1,"There are 10 beads, so 4/10 = 2/5 are green. 2/3 compares green with white; 3/5 is the white fraction.","共有 10 颗珠子，绿珠占 4/10 = 2/5。2/3 比较的是绿珠与白珠；3/5 是白珠占整体的分数。","Find the whole before simplifying the fraction.","先求整体，再化简分数。"],["A walker travels 7.5 km in 1.5 hours at a steady pace. What is the speed in km per hour?","步行者以恒定速度在 1.5 小时内走了 7.5 千米。每小时走多少千米？",[["0.2 km/h","0.2 千米/小时"],["11.25 km/h","11.25 千米/小时"],["5 km/h","5 千米/小时"]],2,"7.5 ÷ 1.5 = 5 km/h. 0.2 comes from hours per kilometer; 11.25 multiplies quantities instead of finding distance in one hour.","7.5 ÷ 1.5 = 5 千米/小时。0.2 是每千米所需的小时数；11.25 是相乘，并不是求一小时走的路程。","Distance divided by time gives distance per one hour.","路程除以时间，得到每一小时的路程。"],["A paint mix uses blue : white = 2 : 5. Which change keeps the color the same?","颜料中蓝色 : 白色 = 2 : 5。怎样改变用量仍保持同样的颜色？",[["Use 6 cups blue and 15 cups white","用 6 杯蓝色和 15 杯白色"],["Use 5 cups blue and 8 cups white","用 5 杯蓝色和 8 杯白色"],["Use 4 cups blue and 5 cups white","用 4 杯蓝色和 5 杯白色"]],0,"Multiplying both parts by 3 gives 6 : 15. Adding 3 to both parts gives a different ratio; doubling only blue also changes the color.","两部分都乘以 3，得到 6 : 15。两部分都加 3 会改变比率；只把蓝色加倍也会改变颜色。","Equivalent ratios use the same multiplier on both parts.","等值比的两个部分要乘以同一个数。"],["Juice A costs $2.40 for 600 mL. Juice B costs $3 for 1,000 mL. Which costs less per 100 mL?","果汁 A 每 600 毫升 2.40 美元；果汁 B 每 1,000 毫升 3 美元。哪种每 100 毫升更便宜？",[["A, because its total price is lower","A，因为总价更低"],["B, at $0.30 per 100 mL","B，每 100 毫升 $0.30"],["They cost the same per 100 mL","两种每 100 毫升价格相同"]],1,"A costs $2.40 ÷ 6 = $0.40 per 100 mL; B costs $3 ÷ 10 = $0.30. A's lower total price does not make its unit price lower.","A 每 100 毫升是 $2.40 ÷ 6 = $0.40；B 是 $3 ÷ 10 = $0.30。A 总价低，并不代表单价低。","Divide each price by the number of 100 mL portions.","把每种总价除以所含 100 毫升的份数。"]]},{"lesson":6,"title":"Theme & Main Idea","bg":[["A theme is an interpretation supported by a pattern in a story, not a slogan you can attach to any story. Track a character's problem, choices, and change. A main-idea statement for an informational paragraph should cover its important details without becoming too broad. A topic names the subject; a full statement says something about it.","主题是由故事中的一连串细节支持的解读，不是随便套用的口号。追踪人物的问题、选择和变化。说明性段落的中心思想应概括重要细节，又不能过于宽泛。话题只是指出对象；完整陈述还要说明对象的某个方面。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Follow the evidence:\u003c/b> Nia hides a broken class model because she fears blame. Her group cannot fix it without knowing what happened. When she explains her mistake, they repair it together. The topic is honesty; a supported theme is \u003cb>admitting a mistake can help people solve a problem together\u003c/b>. 'Always win competitions' has no support here.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>跟随证据：\u003c/b>妮娅害怕被责怪，藏起了损坏的班级模型。小组不知道发生了什么，无法修理。她说明错误后，大家一起修好了模型。话题是诚实；有证据支持的主题是\u003cb>承认错误能帮助人们共同解决问题\u003c/b>。“比赛一定要获胜”在这里没有依据。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["topic versus theme","话题与主题的区别","A topic names a subject, such as trust. A theme states a supported insight, such as trust grows through honest actions.","话题指出对象，如信任。主题表达有依据的认识，如诚实的行动能增进信任。"],["scope of a main idea","中心思想的范围","The main idea should cover the important details of this text, without claiming more than those details support.","中心思想应涵盖本文的重要细节，但不能超出细节所支持的范围。"]],"q":[["Mina laughs at a beginner's mistakes. Later, while learning to skate, she feels embarrassed when others laugh. She apologizes to the beginner. Which theme is best supported?","米娜嘲笑初学者的错误。后来她学滑冰，被别人嘲笑时感到难堪。她向那位初学者道歉。哪个主题最有依据？",[["Embarrassment always prevents people from learning","难堪总会阻止人们学习"],["Only experts can understand another person’s difficulty","只有专家才能理解别人的困难"],["Experiencing another person's difficulty can build empathy","亲身体验他人的困难能培养同理心"]],2,"Mina’s experience changes how she treats someone else, supporting empathy. The story does not show that embarrassment always blocks learning or that empathy requires expertise.","米娜的经历改变了她对待别人的方式，支持同理心这个主题。故事没有说明难堪总会阻止学习，也没有说明同理心需要专家水平。","Connect the character's change to a broader insight.","把人物的变化与更普遍的道理联系起来。"],["A paragraph explains that wetlands slow floodwater, filter some pollutants, and provide animal habitats. Which main idea covers all three details?","一段文字说明湿地能减缓洪水、过滤一些污染物并提供动物栖息地。哪个中心思想涵盖这三个细节？",[["Wetlands provide several important environmental benefits","湿地具有多种重要的环境效益"],["Wetlands are useful only to animals","湿地只对动物有用"],["Every wetland removes every pollutant","每片湿地都能清除所有污染物"]],0,"The first statement covers flood control, filtering, and habitat. 'Only animals' leaves out two details; 'every pollutant' overstates 'some pollutants.'","第一项涵盖防洪、过滤和栖息地。“只对动物”遗漏两个细节；“所有污染物”夸大了“一些污染物”。","Choose a statement broad enough for every detail, but no broader than the evidence.","选择能涵盖所有细节、却不超出证据范围的陈述。"],["A reader says a story's theme is 'cooperation.' Which revision turns the topic into a theme statement?","读者说一个故事的主题是“合作”。哪种修改把话题变成了主题陈述？",[["The story has three characters","故事有三个人物"],["People can solve harder problems when they combine different strengths","人们结合各自不同的长处，就能解决更难的问题"],["A group project","一个小组项目"]],1,"A theme states an insight about experience. 'Cooperation' and 'a group project' name topics; counting characters gives a detail, not a message.","主题要表达对生活经验的认识。“合作”和“小组项目”只是话题；人物数量是细节，不是寓意。","A theme should make a complete, supportable statement.","主题应是完整且能由文本支持的陈述。"],["Which detail best supports the theme 'Courage can mean acting even while afraid'?","哪个细节最能支持“勇气可以意味着即使害怕仍采取行动”这个主题？",[["Feeling nervous, the character stays silent about the broken stair","人物因紧张而没有报告破损的楼梯"],["The character calmly describes a safe, repaired stair afterward","人物事后平静地描述已修好的安全楼梯"],["With shaking hands, the character reports a dangerous broken stair","人物双手发抖，却仍报告了危险的破损楼梯"]],2,"Shaking hands show fear; reporting the danger shows action despite it. Remaining silent shows fear without action; calmly describing a repaired stair does not show acting while afraid.","双手发抖表现害怕；报告危险表现虽害怕仍行动。沉默表现恐惧而没有行动；平静描述修好的楼梯没有表现虽害怕仍行动。","Look for both fear and a purposeful action.","同时寻找恐惧和有目的的行动。"]]},{"lesson":11,"title":"Scientific Investigation","bg":[["Write a measurement plan before collecting data: what will be measured, with which tool and units, and at what time? Repeat trials and keep every result, including unexpected ones. Evidence may support a hypothesis or suggest revising it; one experiment does not prove an explanation true for every possible situation.","收集数据前先写测量计划：测什么、用什么工具和单位、什么时候测？重复试验并保留每个结果，包括意外结果。证据可能支持假设，也可能提示需要修改假设；一次实验不能证明一个解释在所有情况下都正确。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Make a fair comparison:\u003c/b> Test how ramp height affects a toy car's travel distance. Use the same car, surface, and release method. Try each height three times and record centimeters. At 10 cm height the distances are 42, 45, and 43 cm; at 20 cm they are 66, 63, and 66 cm. These results support farther travel at the higher ramp \u003cb>in this setup\u003c/b>. They do not prove every car will behave identically.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>公平比较：\u003c/b>研究斜坡高度怎样影响玩具车行驶距离。保持小车、地面和释放方法相同。每个高度试三次，用厘米记录。10 厘米高时距离为 42、45、43 厘米；20 厘米高时为 66、63、66 厘米。结果支持\u003cb>在这个装置中\u003c/b>较高斜坡使车行驶更远，但不能证明所有小车都完全一样。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["measurement plan","测量计划","A description of what to measure, the tool and units, and when or how often to measure it.","说明测量对象、工具、单位，以及何时或多久测量一次的计划。"],["unexpected result","意外结果","A result that differs from a prediction. Record and investigate it; do not erase it just to make the hypothesis look right.","与预测不同的结果。应记录并调查，而不是为让假设看似正确而删掉。"]],"q":[["To test how water temperature affects dissolving time, which plan makes the fairest comparison?","要研究水温如何影响溶解时间，哪个方案最公平？",[["Keep sugar mass, water volume, and stirring the same; change temperature","保持糖的质量、水量和搅拌方式相同，只改变水温"],["Change temperature and use twice as much sugar in warm water","改变水温，并在温水里放两倍的糖"],["Use different powders and different amounts of water","使用不同粉末和不同水量"]],0,"Changing only temperature lets the comparison address temperature. Changing sugar mass, powder, or water volume introduces other possible explanations.","只改变水温，比较结果才能针对水温。改变糖的质量、粉末种类或水量，会引入其他可能的解释。","Which plan changes only the factor being investigated?","哪个方案只改变研究中的因素？"],["A student records 12, 11, and 28 seconds in three trials. What should the student do with 28 seconds?","三次试验记录为 12、11、28 秒。学生应该怎样处理 28 秒？",[["Replace it with 12 so the data agree","改成 12，让数据一致"],["Keep it, check the procedure, and repeat trials if appropriate","保留它，检查步骤，必要时再做试验"],["Delete it because unexpected results are never useful","删掉，因为意外结果没有用"]],1,"An unusual value may reveal variation or a procedural problem. Keeping it and investigating is more reliable than changing or discarding it without a documented reason.","异常数值可能揭示自然变化或操作问题。保留并调查，比没有记录理由就修改或删除更可靠。","Honest records include results that do not match the prediction.","诚实的记录包括不符合预测的结果。"],["A table shows that seeds in Setup A sprouted sooner than seeds in Setup B. Both light and water differed. What can be concluded?","表格显示 A 装置中的种子比 B 装置更早发芽，但光照和水量都不同。能得出什么结论？",[["Light alone caused the difference","只有光照导致了差异"],["Water alone caused the difference","只有水量导致了差异"],["The setups differed in sprouting time, but the cause is not isolated","两装置发芽时间不同，但没有单独确定原因"]],2,"Two factors changed, so the data do not isolate either cause. A follow-up test should change one factor while controlling the other.","两个因素都改变了，所以数据不能单独确定任何一个原因。后续实验应改变一个因素，同时控制另一个因素。","Count how many conditions changed between the setups.","数一数两个装置之间改变了几个条件。"],["Which entry is a measured observation rather than an inference?","哪条记录是测量得到的观察，而不是推断？",[["The thermometer reads 24 °C","温度计读数是 24 °C"],["The plant is unhappy","植物不开心"],["The soil must lack nutrients","土壤一定缺乏养分"]],0,"A thermometer reading is directly measured. 'Unhappy' is not a defined measurement, and a nutrient shortage is an explanation that needs further evidence.","温度计读数是直接测量值。“不开心”不是明确的测量指标；缺少养分是一种解释，需要进一步证据。","Separate what the tool shows from what you think caused it.","区分工具显示的结果与对原因的猜测。"]]},{"lesson":18,"title":"The American Revolution","bg":[["Separate a cause, an event, and an outcome. Disputes over taxation and political authority helped cause the Revolution. The Declaration announced independence in 1776; fighting continued afterward. The 1783 Treaty of Paris formally ended the war with Britain and recognized United States independence. Not every colonist supported independence, and the new nation's promises were not equally available to everyone.","区分原因、事件和结果。围绕税收与政治权力的争议是独立战争的原因之一。1776 年的《独立宣言》宣布独立，但战争此后仍在继续。1783 年《巴黎条约》正式结束了与英国的战争，承认美国独立。并非所有殖民地居民都支持独立，新国家的承诺也没有平等地惠及所有人。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Reason with a timeline:\u003c/b> Place 1776 (Declaration), 1781 (Yorktown), and 1783 (Treaty of Paris) in order. The Declaration states a political claim; Yorktown is a major military victory; the treaty records formal peace and British recognition. Calling all three 'the day independence happened' hides their different roles.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>用时间线推理：\u003c/b>按顺序排列 1776 年（《独立宣言》）、1781 年（约克镇战役）和 1783 年（《巴黎条约》）。宣言表达政治主张；约克镇是重要军事胜利；条约记录正式和平与英国的承认。把三者都说成“独立发生的那一天”，会掩盖它们不同的作用。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["cause and outcome","原因与结果","A cause helps explain why an event happened; an outcome is something that happened because of it.","原因帮助解释事件为何发生；结果是事件带来的后果。"],["formal recognition","正式承认","An official acceptance of a political status, such as Britain's recognition of U.S. independence in the 1783 treaty.","正式接受某种政治地位，如英国在 1783 年条约中承认美国独立。"]],"q":[["Which statement best distinguishes the Declaration of Independence from the Treaty of Paris of 1783?","哪项最准确地区分《独立宣言》和 1783 年《巴黎条约》？",[["Both documents were battle plans","两份文件都是作战计划"],["The Declaration announced independence; the treaty ended the war with Britain and recognized it","宣言宣布独立；条约结束与英国的战争并承认独立"],["The treaty was signed before the Declaration","条约在宣言之前签署"]],1,"The documents had different purposes and dates: announcement in 1776, peace and recognition in 1783. Neither was a battle plan, and 1783 came later.","两份文件目的和日期不同：1776 年宣布独立，1783 年达成和平并获得承认。两者都不是作战计划，1783 年也在后。","Match each document to what it actually did.","把每份文件与它实际发挥的作用对应起来。"],["A historian uses a Patriot pamphlet to study arguments for independence. What is an important limitation?","历史学家用爱国者的小册子研究支持独立的论点。哪项局限值得注意？",[["A source from the time cannot provide evidence","当时的资料不能提供证据"],["The pamphlet proves all colonists agreed","小册子证明所有殖民地居民都赞同"],["It gives one perspective and does not represent every colonist","它提供一种立场，不能代表所有居民"]],2,"The pamphlet is evidence of its author's argument, not proof of unanimous opinion. A contemporary source can be useful while still having a limited perspective.","小册子能证明作者提出的论点，却不能证明意见一致。当时的资料可以有价值，同时也具有立场局限。","Ask whose viewpoint is present and whose is missing.","问一问：谁的观点被呈现了，谁的观点缺席了？"],["Which sequence puts these events in chronological order?","哪个顺序按时间先后排列了这些事件？",[["Declaration of Independence → Yorktown → Treaty of Paris","《独立宣言》→ 约克镇战役 →《巴黎条约》"],["Yorktown → Treaty of Paris → Declaration of Independence","约克镇战役 →《巴黎条约》→《独立宣言》"],["Treaty of Paris → Declaration of Independence → Yorktown","《巴黎条约》→《独立宣言》→ 约克镇战役"]],0,"The dates are 1776, 1781, and 1783. The other sequences place the announcement after later events or peace before the wartime victory.","日期依次为 1776、1781、1783 年。其他顺序把宣言放到了后来的事件之后，或把和平放在战时胜利之前。","Attach a year to each event, then sort the years.","先给每个事件标上年份，再按年份排序。"],["Why is 'Every colonist wanted independence' an inaccurate summary?","为什么“每个殖民地居民都希望独立”是不准确的概括？",[["The colonies had no political disagreements","殖民地没有政治分歧"],["Patriots, Loyalists, and people who remained neutral held different positions","爱国者、效忠派和保持中立的人持有不同立场"],["Independence was discussed only after 1783","独立问题直到 1783 年后才被讨论"]],1,"Colonial society included supporters of independence, supporters of Britain, and people who tried to remain neutral. The word 'every' erases those differences.","殖民地社会中有人支持独立，有人支持英国，也有人试图保持中立。“每个”抹去了这些差异。","Look for a statement that acknowledges more than one viewpoint.","寻找承认多种立场的陈述。"]]},{"lesson":23,"title":"Two-Step Equations","bg":[["An equation is a balance, so each step must act on both entire sides. More than one valid first step may exist. For 3x + 6 = 18, subtracting 6 first is convenient; dividing every term by 3 first also works: x + 2 = 6. Dividing only 3x while leaving +6 unchanged would not preserve equality.","方程像天平，每一步都要对两边完整地进行同样的运算。第一步可能不止一种正确方法。解 3x + 6 = 18 时先减 6 很方便；先把每一项都除以 3 也可以：x + 2 = 6。只把 3x 除以 3 却保持 +6 不变，就不能保持相等。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Build and check a model:\u003c/b> A club pays an $8 delivery fee plus $3 for each notebook. The total is $29. Let n be the number of notebooks: 3n + 8 = 29. Subtract 8 from both sides, then divide by 3: n = 7. Check the context: 7 notebooks cost $21; $21 + $8 = $29. The answer is a count of notebooks, not a dollar amount.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>建模并检验：\u003c/b>社团支付 8 美元配送费，每本笔记本另付 3 美元，总共 29 美元。设本数为 n：3n + 8 = 29。两边减 8，再除以 3，得到 n = 7。结合情境检验：7 本共 21 美元；$21 + $8 = $29。答案是笔记本的本数，不是美元金额。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["equivalent equations","同解方程","Equations with the same solution set. A valid balance-preserving operation keeps the solutions unchanged.","解集相同的方程。保持等式平衡的正确运算不会改变解。"],["substitution check","代入检验","Replace the variable with the proposed answer in the original equation and compare both sides.","把拟定答案代入原方程的变量，比较两边是否相等。"]],"q":[["Solve −3x + 5 = 20.","解方程 −3x + 5 = 20。",[["x = 5","x = 5"],["x = −25/3","x = −25/3"],["x = −5","x = −5"]],2,"Subtract 5: −3x = 15. Divide by −3: x = −5. Positive 5 loses the negative sign; −25/3 comes from adding 5 instead of undoing it.","先减 5：−3x = 15，再除以 −3：x = −5。正 5 丢失了负号；−25/3 是把 5 加上而不是减去的结果。","Undo the addition, then divide by the signed coefficient.","先消去加法，再除以带符号的系数。"],["For 4x + 8 = 28, which is a valid first step?","对于 4x + 8 = 28，哪个第一步正确？",[["Divide every term by 4 to get x + 2 = 7","每一项都除以 4，得到 x + 2 = 7"],["Divide only 4x by 4 to get x + 8 = 28","只把 4x 除以 4，得到 x + 8 = 28"],["Subtract 8 only on the left to get 4x = 28","只在左边减 8，得到 4x = 28"]],0,"Dividing both entire sides gives (4x + 8)/4 = 28/4, or x + 2 = 7. Changing one term or one side alone breaks the balance.","两边整体除以 4，得到 (4x + 8)/4 = 28/4，即 x + 2 = 7。只改变一项或一边会破坏平衡。","Check whether the operation applies to both complete sides.","检查运算是否作用于完整的两边。"],["A museum trip costs $6 for transport plus $4 per ticket. The total is $30. How many tickets were bought?","博物馆之行交通费为 6 美元，每张门票 4 美元，总共 30 美元。买了几张票？",[["9 tickets","9 张"],["6 tickets","6 张"],["7.5 tickets","7.5 张"]],1,"4t + 6 = 30, so 4t = 24 and t = 6. Nine comes from adding the fee before dividing; 7.5 ignores the transport fee.","4t + 6 = 30，所以 4t = 24，t = 6。9 是先加上费用再除的结果；7.5 忽略了交通费。","Remove the one-time fee before dividing by the ticket price.","先去掉一次性费用，再除以每张票价。"],["A learner claims x = 4 solves x/2 − 3 = 1. Which check is correct?","学生说 x = 4 是 x/2 − 3 = 1 的解。哪个检验正确？",[["4/2 − 3 = 1, so the claim is correct","4/2 − 3 = 1，所以正确"],["4 − 3 = 1, so the claim is correct","4 − 3 = 1，所以正确"],["4/2 − 3 = −1, so x = 4 is not a solution","4/2 − 3 = −1，所以 x = 4 不是解"]],2,"Substitute into every part of the original expression: 4/2 − 3 = 2 − 3 = −1. The first option miscalculates; the second drops division by 2.","代入原式的每一部分：4/2 − 3 = 2 − 3 = −1。第一项算错了；第二项漏掉了除以 2。","Use the original equation, including the division.","使用原方程，不要漏掉除法。"]]},{"lesson":29,"title":"Argument & Persuasive Writing","bg":[["Strong arguments connect a specific claim, relevant evidence, and reasoning that explains the connection. Evidence can be accurate yet irrelevant. A survey about favorite colors cannot show whether a bus route is safe. Explain the limits of a source, address a reasonable counterargument, and avoid words such as 'everyone' when the evidence describes only a small group.","有力的论证把具体主张、相关证据和解释两者联系的推理结合起来。证据即使准确，也可能不相关。关于最喜欢颜色的调查，不能说明公交路线是否安全。应解释资料的局限，回应合理的反方观点；证据只涉及一小群人时，不要使用“所有人”等词。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Link evidence to a claim:\u003c/b> Claim: add a water-refill station near the gym. In a fictional school survey, 48 of 60 team members report waiting at the only fountain after practice. Reasoning: another station nearby could reduce the queue. Counterargument: installation costs money. Response: compare installation and maintenance costs with expected use before deciding. The survey shows a concern among these team members, not the opinion of every student.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>把证据与主张相连：\u003c/b>主张：在体育馆附近增加饮水补水点。假设某校调查中，60 名队员有 48 人说训练后要在唯一的饮水台排队。推理：附近增加一个补水点可能缩短队伍。反方观点：安装要花钱。回应：决定前应比较安装和维护成本与预计使用量。调查反映这些队员的困扰，并不代表全校每个人的意见。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["relevance of evidence","证据的相关性","Whether a fact or example actually helps support the particular claim being argued.","事实或例子是否确实有助于支持正在讨论的特定主张。"],["qualified claim","有限定的主张","A claim that states its limits, using words such as some, may, or in this setting when the evidence requires them.","说明适用范围的主张；证据需要时，使用“一些”“可能”或“在此情境中”等限定词。"]],"q":[["The claim is 'Our school should repair the library's broken reading lights.' Which evidence is most relevant?","主张是“学校应该修理图书馆损坏的阅读灯”。哪项证据最相关？",[["A log shows six reading lamps have failed and several desks are poorly lit","记录显示六盏阅读灯坏了，几张书桌照明不足"],["Library records show which books were borrowed most often","图书馆记录显示哪些书最常被借阅"],["A survey identifies students’ favorite book genres","调查指出学生最喜欢的书籍类型"]],0,"The lamp log directly supports the need for repairs. Borrowing records and genre preferences concern reading but do not establish a lighting problem.","灯具记录直接支持维修的必要性。借阅记录和类型喜好与阅读有关，却不能说明照明问题。","Ask which fact would help a decision about the lights.","问哪个事实有助于决定是否维修阅读灯。"],["A writer says, 'Twenty students used the new study room, so every student prefers it.' What is the best revision?","作者说：“20 名学生用了新自习室，所以每个学生都更喜欢它。”怎样修改最好？",[["Everyone certainly prefers it because it is new","因为它是新的，所以每个人肯定更喜欢"],["At least twenty students used it; broader feedback is needed to judge preferences","至少 20 名学生使用过；判断偏好还需要更广泛的反馈"],["No student likes it","没有学生喜欢它"]],1,"Usage by twenty students does not establish everyone's preference. The qualified revision stays within the evidence; both absolute claims go beyond it.","20 人使用过不能证明所有人的偏好。有限定的修改没有超出证据；两个绝对化判断都超出了证据。","Match the size of the claim to what was actually observed.","让主张的范围与实际观察到的事实相符。"],["Which sentence provides reasoning after the evidence 'The shaded benches were cooler than the unshaded benches at noon'?","证据是“中午有遮阴的长椅比没有遮阴的更凉”。哪句话提供了推理？",[["The bench temperatures were recorded at noon","长椅温度是在中午记录的"],["The park has more unshaded benches than shaded benches","公园没有遮阴的长椅比有遮阴的多"],["Adding shade may make the seating area more comfortable during hot lunch periods","增加遮阴可能让炎热午餐时段的座位区更舒适"]],2,"The third sentence connects the temperature evidence to a proposal. Repeating the measurement time or counting benches does not explain how the temperature evidence supports adding shade.","第三句把温度证据与建议联系起来。重复测量时间或统计长椅数量，都没有解释温度证据怎样支持增加遮阴。","Reasoning explains why the evidence matters to the claim.","推理说明证据为什么与主张有关。"],["A proposal for a school garden faces the concern 'Who will water it during holidays?' Which response addresses the concern?","校园花园提案遇到质疑：“放假期间谁来浇水？”哪个回应真正处理了质疑？",[["Suggest a volunteer schedule and check whether enough adults can commit","提出志愿者轮值表，并确认是否有足够成年人承诺参加"],["Say people who ask questions hate plants","说提出问题的人讨厌植物"],["Repeat that gardens are beautiful","重复花园很美"]],0,"A staffing plan responds to the practical objection and can be checked. Attacking the questioner or repeating an unrelated benefit avoids the concern.","人员计划回应了实际问题，而且可以核实。攻击提问者或重复无关的好处，都回避了质疑。","Answer the other side's strongest practical reason.","回应对方最有力的实际理由。"]]},{"lesson":34,"title":"DNA, Genes & Heredity","bg":[["For a simple one-gene model, a genotype is the allele combination and a phenotype is the observed trait. If A is completely dominant to a, AA and Aa show the dominant phenotype, while aa shows the recessive phenotype. This model is useful, but many real traits involve multiple genes and environmental effects. Dominant does not mean stronger, better, or more common.","在简单的单基因模型中，基因型是等位基因组合，表现型是可观察到的性状。若 A 对 a 完全显性，AA 和 Aa 都表现显性性状，aa 表现隐性性状。这个模型有用，但许多真实性状涉及多个基因及环境影响。显性不代表更强、更好或更常见。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Read probability correctly:\u003c/b> In the simple cross Aa × Aa, each parent can pass on A or a. The four equally likely combinations are AA, Aa, aA, and aa. Three show the dominant phenotype and one the recessive phenotype. A 1/4 chance of aa applies to each offspring; it does \u003cb>not\u003c/b> guarantee exactly one aa offspring in a group of four.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>正确理解概率：\u003c/b>在简单的 Aa × Aa 杂交中，每个亲本可传递 A 或 a。四种等可能组合是 AA、Aa、aA、aa。三种表现显性，一种表现隐性。每个后代为 aa 的概率是 1/4；这\u003cb>不保证\u003c/b>每四个后代中恰好有一个 aa。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["genotype–phenotype distinction","基因型与表现型的区别","Genotype describes an allele combination; phenotype describes an observed trait. Different genotypes can share a phenotype.","基因型描述等位基因组合，表现型描述可观察性状。不同基因型可能具有相同表现型。"],["independent inheritance chance","每次遗传的独立概率","In a simple model, an earlier offspring's outcome does not force the next offspring to have a particular genotype.","在简单模型中，前一个后代的结果不会迫使下一个后代具有某种基因型。"]],"q":[["In a simple model where A is completely dominant to a, which genotype has the recessive phenotype?","在 A 对 a 完全显性的简单模型中，哪个基因型表现隐性性状？",[["AA","AA"],["aa","aa"],["Aa","Aa"]],1,"The recessive phenotype appears with two recessive alleles, aa. AA and Aa both include A and show the dominant phenotype in this model.","两个隐性等位基因 aa 才表现隐性性状。AA 和 Aa 都含 A，在这个模型中表现显性性状。","Check whether a dominant allele is present.","检查是否存在显性等位基因。"],["For Aa × aa in a simple complete-dominance model, what fraction of offspring are expected to be aa?","在完全显性的简单模型中，Aa × aa 的后代预计有多少比例是 aa？",[["1/4","1/4"],["All of them","全部"],["1/2","1/2"]],2,"The first parent passes A or a; the second always passes a. The equally likely combinations are Aa and aa, so half are aa. One quarter applies to Aa × Aa, not this cross.","第一个亲本传 A 或 a，第二个总传 a。等可能组合为 Aa 和 aa，所以一半是 aa。1/4 适用于 Aa × Aa，不适用于本题。","List the allele each parent can contribute.","列出每个亲本能提供的等位基因。"],["A pair of Aa parents has three offspring with the dominant phenotype. In the same simple model, what is the chance the next offspring is aa?","一对 Aa 亲本已有三个表现显性性状的后代。在同一简单模型中，下一个后代为 aa 的概率是多少？",[["1/4","1/4"],["1, because the recessive outcome is now due","1，因为现在该出现隐性了"],["0, because the first three were dominant","0，因为前三个都是显性"]],0,"Each offspring still has a 1/4 chance of aa. Earlier outcomes do not make an outcome 'due' or impossible.","每个后代为 aa 的概率仍是 1/4。先前结果不会使某个结果变成“该出现了”或“不可能”。","A probability is not a promise about a fixed group of four.","概率不是对每四个后代结果的保证。"],["Two plants have the same genotype but receive very different amounts of light and water. Why might their heights differ?","两株植物基因型相同，但光照和水量很不一样。为什么高度可能不同？",[["A genotype guarantees identical height in every environment","基因型保证在任何环境中高度都相同"],["Environmental conditions can influence the phenotype","环境条件可以影响表现型"],["The taller plant must have become a different species","较高的植物一定变成了另一物种"]],1,"Growth can be influenced by both genes and environment. Different height does not by itself show different species, and genotype alone does not fix every outcome.","生长可同时受基因与环境影响。高度不同本身不能证明物种不同，基因型也不能单独决定所有结果。","Consider influences beyond the allele combination.","考虑等位基因组合之外的影响。"]]},{"lesson":40,"title":"The Civil Rights Movement","bg":[["Civil rights change involved many people and methods: court cases, local organizing, boycotts, student sit-ins, marches, and legislation. Distinguish a court ruling from a law passed by Congress, and distinguish a legal change from its enforcement in daily life. A ruling or law could be an important victory while resistance and unequal treatment continued.","民权变化涉及许多人和方法：诉讼、社区组织、抵制、学生静坐、游行和立法。要区分法院裁决与国会通过的法律，也要区分法律变化与日常落实。裁决或法律可能是重要胜利，但抵制和不平等待遇仍可能继续。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Compare methods:\u003c/b> Brown v. Board of Education (1954) was a Supreme Court decision against racial segregation in public schools. The Civil Rights Act (1964) was legislation addressing discrimination in areas including public accommodations and employment. The Voting Rights Act (1965) targeted racial discrimination in voting. These were related advances with different institutions and purposes, supported by sustained organizing.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>比较方法：\u003c/b>1954 年“布朗诉教育委员会案”是最高法院反对公立学校种族隔离的裁决。1964 年《民权法》是处理公共服务场所、就业等领域歧视的立法。1965 年《投票权法》针对投票中的种族歧视。这些进展相互关联，却涉及不同机构和目的，并受到持续组织行动的推动。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["legal change and enforcement","法律变化与执行","Changing a rule and making that rule effective in people's lives are related but different tasks.","改变规则与让规则在人们生活中真正生效，是相关但不同的任务。"],["grassroots organizing","基层组织行动","People in a community working together over time to pursue a shared change.","社区中的人们长期协作，争取共同的改变。"]],"q":[["Which comparison correctly describes Brown v. Board of Education and the Civil Rights Act of 1964?","哪项正确比较了“布朗诉教育委员会案”和 1964 年《民权法》？",[["Both were laws passed by state legislatures","两者都是州议会通过的法律"],["Both were speeches by one movement leader","两者都是同一位运动领袖的演讲"],["Brown was a Supreme Court ruling; the act was a law passed by Congress","布朗案是最高法院裁决；民权法是国会通过的法律"]],2,"The ruling came from the judicial branch; the law came through the federal legislative process. Neither description as state laws or speeches fits.","裁决来自司法部门；法律经过联邦立法程序。把它们说成州法律或演讲都不正确。","Identify the institution that produced each action.","辨认每项行动由哪个机构作出。"],["Why did a bus boycott put pressure on a segregated bus system?","为什么抵制乘坐公交会对实行种族隔离的公交系统形成压力？",[["Participants withheld fares and showed organized opposition","参与者停止支付车费，并表现出有组织的反对"],["A boycott automatically rewrote the Constitution","抵制会自动改写宪法"],["Participants were asking for more segregated seats","参与者要求增加隔离座位"]],0,"Refusing to ride reduced fare income and made collective opposition visible. A boycott did not itself amend the Constitution, and its goal was to challenge segregation.","拒绝乘车减少了票款收入，也让集体反对清楚可见。抵制本身不会修改宪法，其目标是挑战种族隔离。","Connect the action to its economic and public effects.","把行动与其经济影响、公共影响联系起来。"],["A textbook says, 'Once a civil rights law passed, discrimination ended immediately.' What is the best evaluation?","课本说：“民权法律一通过，歧视就立刻结束了。”怎样评价最准确？",[["Correct: laws always change every person's behavior instantly","正确，法律总能立刻改变每个人的行为"],["Too broad: legal protection still required enforcement and continued action","过于绝对：法律保护仍需要执行和持续行动"],["Correct: enforcement was never needed","正确，从来不需要执行"]],1,"A law can establish protection without eliminating all resistance or unfair treatment at once. Enforcement and community action remained important.","法律能确立保护，却不能一次消除所有抵制或不公。执行和社区行动仍然重要。","Distinguish what a law requires from what everyone actually does.","区分法律要求与人们的实际行为。"],["Which historical source would best help investigate how local people organized a civil rights march?","哪种历史资料最有助于研究当地人如何组织民权游行？",[["A later textbook summary of national civil rights laws","后来教科书对全国民权法律的概述"],["An editorial supporting the march but giving no details about its planning","支持游行、却没有筹备细节的社论"],["Organizers' meeting notes, compared with participants' accounts","组织者的会议记录，并与参与者叙述互相比较"]],2,"Meeting notes can document planning, and participant accounts can provide another perspective. A national law summary and a supportive editorial provide context or opinion but less direct evidence of local planning.","会议记录可记载筹备过程，参与者叙述提供另一视角。全国法律概述和支持性的社论能提供背景或意见，但对当地筹备过程的直接证据较少。","Choose sources tied to the question, then compare perspectives.","选择与问题有关的资料，再比较不同视角。"]]},{"lesson":44,"title":"Linear Equations & Slope","bg":[["Use signed changes, not just lengths: slope = change in y divided by change in x. Subtract coordinates in the same order in the numerator and denominator. A horizontal line has slope 0; a vertical line has undefined slope because its change in x is 0. In a real situation, name the slope's units, such as liters per minute.","使用带符号的变化量，不只是长度：斜率 = y 的变化量除以 x 的变化量。分子和分母中的坐标要按相同顺序相减。水平线斜率为 0；竖直线的 x 变化量为 0，所以斜率未定义。在实际情境中应写出单位，如升/分钟。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Interpret a decreasing line:\u003c/b> A tank starts with 18 liters and drains 3 liters each minute: V = 18 − 3t. The intercept 18 is the starting volume; the slope −3 means the volume decreases by 3 liters per minute. After 4 minutes V = 6 liters. The model reaches 0 at 6 minutes; continuing it to negative volumes would not describe this tank.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>解释下降的直线：\u003c/b>水箱起初有 18 升水，每分钟排出 3 升：V = 18 − 3t。截距 18 是初始水量，斜率 −3 表示每分钟减少 3 升。4 分钟后 V = 6 升，6 分钟时到 0。继续算出负水量就不再符合这个水箱的情境。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["signed rate of change","带符号的变化率","A positive rate indicates increase as the input increases; a negative rate indicates decrease. Include the units.","当输入增加时，正变化率表示增加，负变化率表示减少。要写明单位。"],["limits of a linear model","线性模型的适用范围","The input values for which the equation makes sense in its situation, such as stopping a draining-tank model when the tank is empty.","方程在情境中有意义的输入范围，例如排水模型只用到水箱排空为止。"]],"q":[["What is the slope through (1, 7) and (4, 1)?","经过 (1, 7) 和 (4, 1) 的直线斜率是多少？",[["−2","−2"],["2","2"],["−1/2","−1/2"]],0,"(1 − 7)/(4 − 1) = −6/3 = −2. Positive 2 loses the direction of change; −1/2 reverses rise and run.","(1 − 7)/(4 − 1) = −6/3 = −2。正 2 丢失了变化方向；−1/2 颠倒了纵向与横向变化量。","Use the same point order for both differences.","两个差都按同一顺序使用点的坐标。"],["A line passes through (3, 2) and (3, 8). What is its slope?","直线经过 (3, 2) 和 (3, 8)。其斜率是多少？",[["0","0"],["Undefined","未定义"],["6","6"]],1,"The change in x is 0, so the slope would require 6 ÷ 0, which is undefined. Zero slope describes a horizontal line; 6 is only the vertical change.","x 的变化量为 0，计算斜率需要 6 ÷ 0，结果未定义。斜率 0 描述水平线；6 只是纵向变化量。","Calculate the denominator before dividing.","先算分母，再考虑除法。"],["A tank's volume follows V = 24 − 4t, with V in liters and t in minutes, until empty. What does −4 mean?","水箱排空前，水量满足 V = 24 − 4t，V 的单位为升，t 为分钟。−4 表示什么？",[["The tank starts with −4 liters","水箱起初有 −4 升"],["The tank gains 4 liters each minute","水箱每分钟增加 4 升"],["The tank loses 4 liters each minute","水箱每分钟减少 4 升"]],2,"The coefficient of time is the rate: −4 liters per minute. The starting volume is 24, and the negative sign indicates loss, not gain.","时间的系数是变化率：每分钟 −4 升。初始水量是 24，负号表示减少而不是增加。","Separate the starting value from the change per minute.","区分初始值与每分钟的变化量。"],["Which equation represents a line with slope −2 passing through (0, 5)?","哪条方程表示斜率为 −2 且经过 (0, 5) 的直线？",[["y = −2x + 5","y = −2x + 5"],["y = 5x − 2","y = 5x − 2"],["y = 2x + 5","y = 2x + 5"]],0,"The x coefficient is the slope, −2, and the point at x = 0 gives intercept 5. The second swaps the values; the third changes the slope's sign.","x 的系数是斜率 −2；x = 0 时的点给出截距 5。第二项交换了两者，第三项改变了斜率符号。","In y = mx + b, match m to slope and b to the value at x = 0.","在 y = mx + b 中，m 对应斜率，b 对应 x = 0 时的值。"]]},{"lesson":49,"title":"Persuasive Techniques & Media Literacy","bg":[["Before sharing a claim, trace it to its original source, check its date and context, and look for independent evidence. Many reposts of the same claim are not many independent sources. For statistics, ask who was measured, how they were selected, and what comparison was used. A persuasive image can attract attention without proving the words beside it.","分享主张前，追溯原始资料，核查日期和背景，并寻找独立证据。同一主张被大量转发，并不等于有许多独立来源。面对统计数字，要问调查了谁、怎样选人、采用什么比较。吸引人的图片可以抓住注意力，却不能证明旁边的文字。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Check a headline:\u003c/b> 'Club participation doubles!' sounds dramatic. The original figures show a rise from 2 students to 4 students. The increase is 100%, and the absolute increase is 2 students; both descriptions are true. A careful summary includes the starting number and avoids implying that the whole school joined.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>核查标题：\u003c/b>“社团人数翻倍！”听起来很惊人。原始数据从 2 人增到 4 人。增长率是 100%，实际增加了 2 人；两种描述都正确。严谨的概括应包含起始人数，避免暗示全校都加入了。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["independent corroboration","独立印证","Support from a source that did its own reporting or investigation, rather than copying the same original claim.","来自自行报道或调查的资料的支持，而不是重复抄录同一个原始主张。"],["absolute versus relative change","绝对变化与相对变化","Absolute change is the amount added or lost; relative change compares that amount with the starting value.","绝对变化是增加或减少的数量；相对变化是把该数量与起始值比较。"]],"q":[["Ten websites repeat the same unsourced claim word for word. What does this show?","十个网站逐字重复同一个没有来源的主张。这说明什么？",[["There are ten independent investigations","已有十次独立调查"],["The claim has spread, but independent confirmation is still needed","该主张传播了，但仍需要独立核实"],["Repetition makes the claim automatically true","重复会自动使主张变真"]],1,"Copying can spread a claim without adding evidence. Count independent reporting, not just pages repeating the same wording.","复制能传播主张，却不会增加证据。要看独立调查，而不是只数重复相同文字的网页。","Ask whether each source checked the claim itself.","问每个来源是否自行核查过主张。"],["An ad says 'Attendance increased 100%,' from 3 people to 6. Which summary is most complete?","广告说“出席人数增加 100%”，从 3 人变为 6 人。哪个概括最完整？",[["One hundred extra people attended","多来了 100 人"],["Almost everyone in town attended","镇上几乎所有人都来了"],["Attendance doubled, increasing by 3 people","出席人数翻倍，增加了 3 人"]],2,"The relative increase is 3/3 = 100%; the absolute increase is 3 people. Percent is not a head count, and the figures say nothing about the whole town.","相对增长是 3/3 = 100%；绝对增长为 3 人。百分比不是人数，这些数据也不能说明全镇情况。","Report both the starting number and the number added.","同时报告起始人数和增加人数。"],["A photograph from an old flood is shared as proof of flooding today. Which check is most useful?","一张旧洪水照片被当成今天发生洪水的证据分享。哪种核查最有用？",[["Find the original publication, date, and location, then compare current reports","查原始发表记录、日期和地点，再对照当前报道"],["Count how many people liked the post","数帖子获得多少点赞"],["Assume a vivid image must be current","认为鲜明的图片一定是当前的"]],0,"A real photo can be used in a false context. Original date and location help test the claim; popularity and vividness do not establish when it was taken.","真实照片也可能被放在错误背景中。原始日期和地点有助于核查；受欢迎或画面鲜明，都不能证明拍摄时间。","Check the image's context, not just whether it looks real.","核查图片背景，不要只看它是否像真的。"],["A snack company surveys only its fan club and claims 'All students prefer our snack.' What is the strongest concern?","零食公司只调查自己的粉丝俱乐部，却声称“所有学生都更喜欢我们的零食”。最有力的质疑是什么？",[["Companies can never collect any useful information","公司永远不能收集有用信息"],["The selected group may not represent all students","被选中的群体可能不能代表所有学生"],["A longer slogan would prove the claim","更长的标语就能证明主张"]],1,"Fans are especially likely to favor the product. Their responses may describe the fan club but cannot justify a claim about all students; this does not make every company survey useless.","粉丝尤其可能偏爱产品。他们的回答或许反映粉丝群体，却不能支持对所有学生的概括；这也不代表所有公司调查都无用。","Compare the surveyed group with the group named in the claim.","比较被调查群体与主张所指群体。"]]},{"lesson":54,"title":"Chemical Reactions & Conservation of Mass","bg":[["Define the system before comparing masses. In a closed system, matter cannot enter or leave; the total mass is conserved during a chemical reaction. In an open system, gas can escape or oxygen can enter, changing the measured mass of what remains. Atoms are rearranged in ordinary chemical reactions, not created or destroyed. Include containers consistently when weighing before and after.","比较质量前先界定系统。在封闭系统中，物质不能进出，化学反应前后总质量守恒。在开放系统中，气体可能逸出或氧气进入，使留下部分的实测质量改变。普通化学反应中，原子只是重新排列，不会凭空产生或消失。反应前后称量时，要一致地计入容器。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Account for everything:\u003c/b> A sealed container and its contents weigh 125 g before a fizzing reaction. Afterward they should still weigh about 125 g, within measurement uncertainty. If the lid is opened and 2 g of gas escapes, the remaining container and contents may weigh 123 g. The missing 2 g is outside the measured system, not destroyed.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>把所有物质计入：\u003c/b>密闭容器及其内容物在起泡反应前共重 125 克。反应后，在测量误差范围内仍应约为 125 克。如果打开盖子，逸出 2 克气体，留下的容器及内容物可能重 123 克。这 2 克到了测量系统之外，并没有消失。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["system boundary","系统边界","The boundary defining what is included in a measurement. Matter crossing it must be considered in a mass comparison.","界定测量中包含哪些物体的边界。比较质量时必须考虑穿过边界的物质。"],["atom balance","原子数平衡","In an ordinary chemical reaction, each element has the same number of atoms before and after, although the atoms are rearranged.","普通化学反应前后，各元素的原子数相同，但原子的组合方式发生改变。"]],"q":[["A sealed jar and its contents weigh 180 g. A gas-producing reaction occurs without any leak. What mass is expected afterward?","密闭罐及其内容物共重 180 克。在没有泄漏的情况下发生生成气体的反应。反应后预计多重？",[["Less than 180 g because gas has no mass","少于 180 克，因为气体没有质量"],["More than 180 g because bubbles create atoms","多于 180 克，因为气泡创造原子"],["About 180 g, within measurement uncertainty","在测量误差范围内约为 180 克"]],2,"The gas remains inside the closed system and has mass. Bubbles do not create atoms, so the total mass remains the same within measurement limits.","气体仍在封闭系统中，而且有质量。气泡不会创造原子，因此总质量在测量限度内保持相同。","Track whether any matter crosses the boundary.","追踪是否有物质穿过系统边界。"],["A metal sample gains mass as it reacts with oxygen from the air. What best explains the gain?","金属样品与空气中的氧气反应后质量增加。哪个解释最好？",[["Oxygen atoms from outside joined the sample","外界的氧原子加入了样品"],["The reaction created matter from nothing","反应凭空创造了物质"],["Conservation of mass never applies to metals","质量守恒不适用于金属"]],0,"The measured sample gained matter from its surroundings. Including the oxygen that reacted restores the mass accounting; matter was not created.","被测样品从周围获得了物质。把参与反应的氧气计入，就能完整核算质量；没有凭空创造物质。","Include the gas that entered the sample.","把进入样品的气体计入。"],["Before a reaction, a closed system contains 4 hydrogen atoms and 2 oxygen atoms. Which atom count is possible afterward?","反应前，封闭系统中有 4 个氢原子和 2 个氧原子。反应后哪种原子数可能正确？",[["2 hydrogen and 1 oxygen","2 个氢原子和 1 个氧原子"],["4 hydrogen and 2 oxygen, in new combinations","4 个氢原子和 2 个氧原子，形成新的组合"],["4 carbon and 2 oxygen","4 个碳原子和 2 个氧原子"]],1,"Ordinary chemical reactions conserve each kind of atom. They can rearrange these atoms into water molecules, but cannot delete half the atoms or turn hydrogen into carbon.","普通化学反应保持每种原子的数量。可以把这些原子重组为水分子，但不能删去一半原子，也不能把氢变成碳。","Count each element separately before and after.","分别统计反应前后每种元素的原子数。"],["An open cup loses 3 g during a fizzing reaction. Which next investigation best checks the explanation that gas escaped?","开放杯中的起泡反应使称得的质量减少 3 克。哪个后续研究最能检验“气体逸出”的解释？",[["Ignore all gas because only solids have mass","忽略所有气体，因为只有固体有质量"],["Use a different balance only after the reaction","只在反应后换一台天平"],["Repeat with a suitable sealed setup that captures the gas and weigh the whole setup","用能收集气体的适当密闭装置重复实验，并称整个装置"]],2,"Capturing and weighing the gas keeps it inside the measured system. Ignoring gas misses matter; changing the balance between measurements introduces a new uncertainty.","收集并称量气体，使它留在被测系统内。忽略气体会漏掉物质；前后换天平会引入新的不确定因素。","Choose a safe setup that includes all products in the measurement.","选择能把全部生成物计入测量的安全装置。"]]},{"lesson":60,"title":"The Constitution & Branches of Government","bg":[["Two different kinds of division matter. Separation of powers divides national responsibilities among legislative, executive, and judicial branches. Federalism divides authority between national and state governments. Checks and balances let branches limit one another; they do not mean that each branch performs exactly the same job.","两种权力划分方式都很重要。三权分立把联邦职责分给立法、行政和司法部门。联邦制在联邦与州政府之间划分权力。制衡使各部门能够限制其他部门；这不表示每个部门都做完全相同的工作。"]],"ex":["\u003cp>\u003cb>Trace a check:\u003c/b> Congress passes a bill; the president vetoes it; two-thirds of both the House and Senate vote to override. The veto checks Congress, and the override checks the president. This example concerns branches of the national government, not a division between national and state governments.\u003c/p>","\u003cp>\u003cb>追踪一次制衡：\u003c/b>国会通过法案，总统否决，随后参议院和众议院各以三分之二多数推翻否决。否决约束国会，推翻否决又约束总统。这个例子涉及联邦政府的不同部门，而不是联邦与州政府之间的划分。\u003c/p>"],"v":[["branch versus level of government","政府部门与政府层级","A branch is legislative, executive, or judicial; a level is national, state, or local. These are different ways to describe government.","部门指立法、行政或司法；层级指联邦、州或地方。这是描述政府的不同方式。"],["veto override","推翻否决","Congress can override a presidential veto with a two-thirds vote in each house.","国会可由参议院和众议院各以三分之二多数推翻总统否决。"]],"q":[["Which example describes federalism rather than separation of powers?","哪个例子描述联邦制，而不是三权分立？",[["The national government and state governments each exercise constitutional authority","联邦政府与州政府各自行使宪法规定的权力"],["Congress makes laws while federal courts interpret them","国会制定法律，联邦法院解释法律"],["The president vetoes a bill passed by Congress","总统否决国会通过的法案"]],0,"Federalism concerns national and state levels. Different jobs within the national government show separation of powers; a veto is a check between branches.","联邦制涉及联邦与州两个层级。联邦政府内部的不同职责体现三权分立；否决是部门之间的制衡。","Ask whether the example compares levels or branches.","问这个例子比较的是层级还是部门。"],["The president vetoes a bill. What must Congress do to override the veto?","总统否决一项法案。国会怎样才能推翻否决？",[["Win a simple majority in only the House","只在众议院获得简单多数"],["Win a two-thirds vote in both the House and the Senate","参议院和众议院都获得三分之二多数"],["Ask one member of Congress to sign the bill","请一名国会议员签署法案"]],1,"An override requires the two-thirds threshold in each house. One chamber alone, a simple majority, or one member's signature is insufficient.","推翻否决要求两院各达到三分之二门槛。只有一个议院、简单多数或一名议员签字都不够。","The threshold applies separately to both chambers.","门槛分别适用于两个议院。"],["Why does judicial review act as a check on the other branches?","为什么司法审查能制约其他部门？",[["It lets courts write every law without Congress","它让法院无需国会就制定所有法律"],["It lets courts ignore the Constitution","它让法院无视宪法"],["It allows courts to decide whether laws or government actions conflict with the Constitution","它允许法院判断法律或政府行为是否违反宪法"]],2,"Review tests government action against the Constitution. It does not make courts the legislature or place them above the Constitution.","司法审查依据宪法检验政府行为。它不会把法院变成立法机关，也不会让法院凌驾于宪法之上。","A check limits power by applying a constitutional standard.","制衡通过适用宪法标准来限制权力。"],["A student says, 'Checks and balances means every branch can do exactly the same things.' Which correction is best?","学生说：“制衡意味着每个部门都能做完全相同的事。”哪个纠正最好？",[["Branches have different responsibilities and specific ways to limit one another","各部门职责不同，并有特定方式限制其他部门"],["Only one branch has any power","只有一个部门拥有权力"],["State governments are the three national branches","州政府就是联邦的三个部门"]],0,"Checks work alongside distinct responsibilities. They do not erase the branches or turn levels of government into branches.","制衡与不同职责并存。它不会消除部门区别，也不会把政府层级变成部门。","Separate the job of a branch from its checks on another branch.","区分一个部门的职责与它对另一部门的制约。"]]}],"wrong":{"0:7:0":["2/3 compares green beads with white beads, not green with all 10 beads.","2/3 比较绿珠与白珠，而不是绿珠与全部 10 颗珠子。"],"0:7:2":["3/5 is 6/10, the fraction of white beads, not green beads.","3/5 是 6/10，表示白珠而不是绿珠所占的分数。"],"0:8:0":["0.2 is hours per kilometer; the question asks for kilometers per hour.","0.2 是每千米的小时数；题目问每小时的千米数。"],"0:8:1":["11.25 comes from multiplying 7.5 by 1.5; divide distance by time to find speed.","11.25 是 7.5 乘以 1.5；求速度应把路程除以时间。"],"0:9:1":["Adding 3 to both parts changes 2 : 5 into 5 : 8; equivalent ratios need a shared multiplier.","两部分都加 3 会把 2 : 5 变成 5 : 8；等值比需要同乘一个数。"],"0:9:2":["Only the blue amount doubled, so blue makes up a larger share of the paint.","只有蓝色加倍，蓝色在颜料中所占比例变大了。"],"0:10:0":["A's smaller bottle costs less overall but more per 100 mL: $0.40 compared with $0.30.","A 的小瓶总价较低，但每 100 毫升是 $0.40，高于 B 的 $0.30。"],"0:10:2":["The unit prices differ: A is $0.40 and B is $0.30 per 100 mL.","单价不同：每 100 毫升 A 为 $0.40，B 为 $0.30。"],"6:7:0":["The story does not establish that embarrassment always stops learning; Mina learns from the experience.","故事没有证明难堪总会阻止学习；米娜从这次经历中学到了东西。"],"6:7:1":["Mina gains understanding while she is a beginner, so expertise is not required for empathy.","米娜在自己还是初学者时就获得了理解，因此同理心不需要专家水平。"],"6:8:1":["'Only to animals' leaves out slowing floodwater and filtering pollutants.","“只对动物”遗漏了减缓洪水和过滤污染物。"],"6:8:2":["The paragraph says 'some pollutants,' not that every pollutant is removed.","段落说的是“一些污染物”，并非所有污染物都能被清除。"],"6:9:0":["Counting characters supplies a detail, not an insight about cooperation.","人物数量是细节，不是关于合作的认识。"],"6:9:2":["'A group project' names a topic; it does not state what the story suggests about it.","“小组项目”只是话题，没有说明故事对它表达了什么认识。"],"6:10:0":["This detail shows fear but no action to address the danger.","这个细节表现害怕，但没有行动来处理危险。"],"6:10:1":["A calm description after the repair does not demonstrate action while afraid.","修好之后平静地描述，没有体现虽害怕仍行动。"],"11:7:1":["Changing both sugar mass and temperature makes it unclear which caused a difference.","同时改变糖的质量和水温，就无法确定差异由哪个因素造成。"],"11:7:2":["Different powders and water volumes add uncontrolled differences.","不同粉末和水量增加了未控制的差异。"],"11:8:0":["Replacing a measured value to fit the pattern falsifies the record.","为符合规律而替换测量值，会使记录失真。"],"11:8:2":["Unexpected results can reveal variation or errors and should be investigated, not automatically deleted.","意外结果可能揭示变化或错误，应调查而不是自动删除。"],"11:9:0":["Because water also changed, these data do not isolate light's effect.","水量也改变了，因此这些数据不能单独确定光照的影响。"],"11:9:1":["Because light also changed, these data do not isolate water's effect.","光照也改变了，因此这些数据不能单独确定水量的影响。"],"11:10:1":["'Unhappy' is an interpretation without a defined measurement.","“不开心”是没有明确测量指标的解释。"],"11:10:2":["A nutrient shortage is a proposed cause, not something directly shown by this observation.","缺乏养分是提出的原因，不是这次观察直接显示的结果。"],"18:7:0":["These documents announced a political position and recorded peace; they were not battle plans.","这些文件宣布政治立场、记录和平，不是作战计划。"],"18:7:2":["The Declaration was in 1776; the Treaty of Paris was later, in 1783.","宣言在 1776 年，巴黎条约更晚，在 1783 年。"],"18:8:0":["A contemporary pamphlet can provide evidence of its author's views and arguments.","当时的小册子能提供作者观点和论据的证据。"],"18:8:1":["One Patriot's argument cannot establish that Loyalists and other colonists agreed.","一个爱国者的论点不能证明效忠派和其他居民都赞同。"],"18:9:1":["The 1776 Declaration came before Yorktown in 1781 and the treaty in 1783.","1776 年宣言先于 1781 年约克镇战役和 1783 年条约。"],"18:9:2":["The 1783 treaty followed both the 1776 Declaration and the 1781 victory.","1783 年条约晚于 1776 年宣言和 1781 年胜利。"],"18:10:0":["Patriots and Loyalists disagreed over independence and loyalty to Britain.","爱国者和效忠派在独立及效忠英国的问题上存在分歧。"],"18:10:2":["The Declaration announced independence in 1776, well before 1783.","1776 年宣言就宣布了独立，远早于 1783 年。"],"23:7:0":["Dividing 15 by −3 gives −5, not positive 5.","15 除以 −3 得 −5，不是正 5。"],"23:7:1":["To undo +5, subtract 5 from 20; adding 5 gives the wrong intermediate value.","消去 +5 应从 20 中减 5；加 5 会得到错误的中间值。"],"23:8:1":["Dividing one term alone changes the equation; divide the entire left and right sides.","只除一项会改变方程；应把完整的左边和右边都除以同一个数。"],"23:8:2":["Subtracting only on the left breaks equality; the right side must also decrease by 8.","只在左边减会破坏相等关系；右边也必须减 8。"],"23:9:0":["Nine tickets would cost $36 plus $6, exceeding the $30 total.","9 张票要 $36，再加 $6，超过 $30 总额。"],"23:9:2":["30 ÷ 4 ignores the $6 transport fee; subtract that fee first.","30 ÷ 4 忽略了 $6 交通费；应先减去这笔费用。"],"23:10:0":["4/2 − 3 equals 2 − 3 = −1, not 1.","4/2 − 3 等于 2 − 3 = −1，不是 1。"],"23:10:1":["This check drops the division by 2 from the original equation.","这个检验漏掉了原方程中的除以 2。"],"29:7:1":["Popular-book records concern reading interests, not whether lamps need repair.","热门书籍记录与阅读兴趣有关，不能说明灯是否需要维修。"],"29:7:2":["Genre preferences do not provide evidence about the condition of the lights.","书籍类型喜好没有提供阅读灯状况的证据。"],"29:8:0":["Being new does not prove that every student prefers the room.","新建不等于每个学生都更喜欢这个房间。"],"29:8:2":["The evidence does not show that nobody likes it; it only records use by twenty students.","证据没有说明无人喜欢；只记录了 20 人使用过。"],"29:9:0":["Repeating the measurement time does not explain why cooler temperatures support adding shade.","重复测量时间，没有解释为何较低温度支持增加遮阴。"],"29:9:1":["The number of benches may be relevant background, but it does not explain the temperature evidence.","长椅数量可以作为相关背景，但没有解释温度证据。"],"29:10:1":["Attacking the questioner does not solve the holiday watering problem.","攻击提问者并不能解决假期浇水问题。"],"29:10:2":["Beauty is a possible benefit but does not identify who will water the garden.","美观可能是好处，但没有说明谁来浇水。"],"34:7:0":["AA includes dominant alleles and shows the dominant phenotype in this model.","AA 含显性等位基因，在这个模型中表现显性性状。"],"34:7:2":["Aa includes A, so it shows the dominant phenotype under complete dominance.","Aa 含 A，在完全显性条件下表现显性性状。"],"34:8:0":["One quarter is the aa probability for Aa × Aa; the second parent here is aa.","四分之一是 Aa × Aa 中 aa 的概率；本题第二个亲本是 aa。"],"34:8:1":["The Aa parent can also pass A, producing Aa rather than aa.","Aa 亲本也可以传 A，产生 Aa 而不是 aa。"],"34:9:1":["Earlier offspring do not make the recessive outcome certain or 'due.'","先前后代的结果不会使隐性结果成为必然或“该出现”。"],"34:9:2":["Three earlier dominant phenotypes do not remove the next offspring's aa possibility.","前三个表现显性，不会消除下一个后代为 aa 的可能。"],"34:10:0":["Environmental conditions can change growth even when genotypes match.","即使基因型相同，环境条件也能改变生长情况。"],"34:10:2":["A difference in height alone does not establish that plants belong to different species.","仅凭高度不同，不能认定植物属于不同物种。"],"40:7:0":["Brown was a federal Supreme Court ruling, and the act was federal legislation.","布朗案是联邦最高法院裁决，民权法是联邦立法。"],"40:7:1":["A court ruling and a statute are institutional actions, not speeches.","法院裁决与法律是机构行动，不是演讲。"],"40:8:1":["A boycott applies public and economic pressure; it does not automatically amend the Constitution.","抵制施加公共与经济压力，不会自动修宪。"],"40:8:2":["The boycott challenged segregation rather than asking for more segregated seating.","抵制是在挑战种族隔离，而不是要求增加隔离座位。"],"40:9:0":["A legal requirement does not instantly change everyone's behavior or remove resistance.","法律要求不会立刻改变所有人的行为或消除抵制。"],"40:9:2":["Enforcement is needed to make legal protections effective.","法律保护要有效落实，就需要执行。"],"40:10:0":["A national overview may explain laws but is less direct evidence of how this local march was planned.","全国概述可能解释法律，但对这次当地游行如何筹备的直接证据较少。"],"40:10:1":["Support for a march reveals an opinion, but this editorial gives no planning details.","支持游行反映一种意见，但这篇社论没有筹备细节。"],"44:7:1":["As x increases from 1 to 4, y falls from 7 to 1, so the slope is negative.","x 从 1 增至 4 时，y 从 7 降至 1，因此斜率为负。"],"44:7:2":["−1/2 reverses the fraction; slope is change in y divided by change in x.","−1/2 把分数颠倒了；斜率是 y 变化量除以 x 变化量。"],"44:8:0":["Zero slope belongs to a horizontal line; these points share x, making a vertical line.","零斜率属于水平线；这些点 x 相同，形成竖直线。"],"44:8:2":["Six is the change in y, but dividing by the zero change in x is undefined.","6 是 y 的变化量，但除以 x 的零变化量未定义。"],"44:9:0":["The starting volume is 24 liters, the value when t = 0.","初始水量为 24 升，是 t = 0 时的值。"],"44:9:1":["The negative coefficient means volume decreases, not increases.","负系数表示水量减少，不是增加。"],"44:10:1":["This equation has slope 5 and intercept −2, reversing the given roles.","这个方程斜率为 5、截距为 −2，把给定的作用颠倒了。"],"44:10:2":["This equation's positive slope makes it rise instead of having slope −2.","这个方程的正斜率使直线上升，并不是斜率 −2。"],"49:7:0":["Identical copied wording does not show that ten investigations occurred.","相同的复制文字不能证明进行了十次调查。"],"49:7:2":["Repetition increases visibility, not the amount of evidence supporting a claim.","重复增加可见度，不会增加支持主张的证据。"],"49:8:0":["A 100% increase describes a proportion, not one hundred additional people.","增加 100% 描述比例，不是增加 100 人。"],"49:8:1":["The numbers 3 and 6 say nothing about what share of the town attended.","3 和 6 这两个数不能说明全镇有多少比例的人参加。"],"49:9:1":["Likes measure reactions, not the photograph's date or location.","点赞衡量反应，不代表照片的日期或地点。"],"49:9:2":["A vivid photograph may still be old or from a different place.","鲜明的照片仍可能是旧照片，或拍自其他地方。"],"49:10:0":["The concern is this sample's representativeness, not that all company information is useless.","问题在于这个样本是否有代表性，而不是公司信息都无用。"],"49:10:2":["A longer slogan adds words, not evidence about all students.","更长的标语只增加文字，没有增加关于所有学生的证据。"],"54:7:0":["Gas has mass and remains inside the sealed jar.","气体有质量，而且仍留在密闭罐内。"],"54:7:1":["A chemical reaction rearranges atoms; bubbles do not create new atoms.","化学反应重新排列原子；气泡不会创造新原子。"],"54:8:1":["The sample gains oxygen already present in the air; matter is not created from nothing.","样品获得的是空气中原有的氧，物质不是凭空创造的。"],"54:8:2":["Conservation applies; the oxygen entering the measured sample must be included.","质量守恒仍适用；必须计入进入被测样品的氧。"],"54:9:0":["This would lose half the atoms, which an ordinary reaction in a closed system does not do.","这会丢掉一半原子；封闭系统中的普通反应不会这样。"],"54:9:2":["Ordinary chemical reactions cannot turn hydrogen atoms into carbon atoms.","普通化学反应不能把氢原子变成碳原子。"],"54:10:0":["Gas is matter and contributes mass, just as solids and liquids do.","气体是物质，像固体、液体一样具有质量。"],"54:10:1":["Changing measuring instruments between readings introduces a new difference without capturing the gas.","前后更换测量仪器引入新差异，却没有收集气体。"],"60:7:1":["Different responsibilities of Congress and federal courts concern national branches, not levels.","国会与联邦法院的不同职责涉及联邦部门，而非层级。"],"60:7:2":["A presidential veto checks another national branch; it does not divide national and state authority.","总统否决制约另一个联邦部门，并非划分联邦与州的权力。"],"60:8:0":["An override needs two-thirds in each house, not a simple majority in just one.","推翻否决需要两院各三分之二，不是仅一院的简单多数。"],"60:8:2":["One member's signature cannot replace the required votes in both houses.","一名议员的签字不能代替两院所需的投票。"],"60:9:0":["Judicial review does not transfer Congress's lawmaking job to the courts.","司法审查不会把国会的立法职责转交法院。"],"60:9:1":["Judicial review applies the Constitution rather than ignoring it.","司法审查适用宪法，而不是无视宪法。"],"60:10:1":["Power is distributed among branches; checks do not leave just one with power.","权力分配给不同部门；制衡不是只让一个部门拥有权力。"],"60:10:2":["States are a level of government, not the legislative, executive, and judicial branches.","州是政府层级，不是立法、行政和司法三个部门。"]}};
